      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Queene-Like Closet\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 (1672) by Hannah Woolley (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#wooley-1672\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EWooley 1672\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003E243. To make Bisket of Potato-Roots or Parsneps.\u003C/b\u003E Take their Roots boil\u0027d very tender, and beat them in a Mortar with their weight of searced Sugar, then put in a little \u003Ca href=\u0022food-additives.html\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EGum dragon\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E as before, beat them to a Paste, and mould them up with Sugar searced, and make them up in what shape you please, and dry them.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
